{
  "description": "Inputs and settings shared by compare.py (qlpca, pyGifi) and generate_r_ground_truth.R (Gifi). The 'knots' and 'inputs' sections are written by `python compare.py manifest` and must not be edited by hand.",
  "packages": {
    "Gifi": "1.0-0",
    "pyGifi": "git+https://github.com/vam-math/pyGifi@7aa81ed"
  },
  "ndim": 2,
  "datasets": {
    "cylinder_0": {
      "source": "qlpca.datasets.make_cylinder",
      "n": 51,
      "noise": 0.0,
      "random_state": 0,
      "significant_digits": 10,
      "note": "rounded to 10 significant digits: the same input on every platform"
    },
    "cylinder_10": {
      "source": "qlpca.datasets.make_cylinder",
      "n": 51,
      "noise": 0.1,
      "random_state": 0,
      "significant_digits": 10,
      "note": "rounded to 10 significant digits: the same input on every platform"
    },
    "cylinder_25": {
      "source": "qlpca.datasets.make_cylinder",
      "n": 51,
      "noise": 0.25,
      "random_state": 0,
      "significant_digits": 10,
      "note": "rounded to 10 significant digits: the same input on every platform"
    },
    "st_gender": {
      "source": "qlpca.datasets.load_st_gender"
    },
    "neumann": {
      "source": "pygifi.get_dataset('neumann')",
      "note": "loaded from pyGifi at run time; also shipped with Gifi (data(neumann)); never stored in this repository"
    },
    "gas_turbine": {
      "source": "UCI Gas Turbine CO and NOx Emission Data Set, doi:10.24432/C5WC95, CC BY 4.0",
      "url": "https://archive.ics.uci.edu/static/public/551/gas+turbine+co+and+nox+emission+data+set.zip",
      "year": 2015,
      "n": 400,
      "random_state": 2015,
      "variables": [
        "AT",
        "AP",
        "AH",
        "AFDP",
        "GTEP",
        "TIT",
        "TAT",
        "TEY",
        "CDP"
      ],
      "excluded": [
        "CO",
        "NOX"
      ]
    }
  },
  "runs": {
    "knots1": {
      "n_knots": 1,
      "degree": 1,
      "ordinal": false
    },
    "knots2": {
      "n_knots": 2,
      "degree": 1,
      "ordinal": false
    },
    "monotone_deg1": {
      "n_knots": 2,
      "degree": 1,
      "ordinal": true,
      "eps": 1e-08,
      "datasets": [
        "cylinder_0",
        "st_gender",
        "neumann"
      ]
    },
    "monotone_deg2": {
      "n_knots": 2,
      "degree": 2,
      "ordinal": true,
      "eps": 1e-08,
      "datasets": [
        "cylinder_0",
        "st_gender",
        "neumann"
      ],
      "same_model": false
    },
    "defaults": {
      "package_defaults": true,
      "same_model": false
    }
  },
  "fit": {
    "eps": 1e-12,
    "itmax": 100000,
    "defaults_note": "the 'defaults' run uses each package's own defaults (princals: levels='ordinal', a knot at every distinct value, eps=1e-6; qlpca: QLPCA(n_components=2))",
    "monotone_note": "monotone runs use eps=1e-8 and three small data sets: the inner Dykstra loop of princals stops at 1e-6 (coneRegression.R), and with degree 2 one pyGifi fit takes several minutes"
  },
  "tolerances": {
    "unrestricted": {
      "evals": 1e-05,
      "transform_corr": 1e-08,
      "objectscores": 0.0005,
      "loadings": 0.0001
    },
    "monotone": {
      "evals": 0.001,
      "transform_corr": 0.001,
      "objectscores": 0.01,
      "loadings": 0.01
    },
    "defaults": {
      "evals": 0.0001,
      "transform_corr": 0.0001,
      "objectscores": 0.001,
      "loadings": 0.001
    },
    "note": "Both packages stop when the loss changes by less than eps in one iteration, which does not bound the distance to the optimum: with eps=1e-12 the two implementations still differ by about 1e-6 in the eigenvalues and 3e-5 in the object scores. 'transform_corr' is 1 - |correlation| per variable. Runs with same_model=false (defaults; monotone degree 2) fit different models in qlpca and princals: their qlpca differences are reported, not tested; pyGifi vs R is tested in every run."
  },
